      "type": "text",
      "id": "h_35",
      "x": 44,
      "y": 1222,
      "width": 1768,
      "height": 24,
      "text": "HOW EACH LANE REACHES THE MODEL — AND WHY C AND D HAVE TO COLLECT OUT OF BAND",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "seed": 277165,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3770244,
      "updated": 1,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HOW EACH LANE REACHES THE MODEL — AND WHY C AND D HAVE TO COLLECT OUT OF BAND",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "angle": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "strokeColor": "#1b1b1b",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "type": "text",
      "id": "b_36",
      "x": 44,
      "y": 1256,
      "width": 1768,
      "height": 159,
      "text": "Lane C — Power BI cannot query the Purview audit API directly: it is POST-only with an Entra audience the Web connector cannot mint.\nLane D — the names live in one Dataverse per environment. Power Query treats 742 endpoints as a dynamic data source and will not refresh them.\nLane D needs a Dataverse application user in every environment first — a second shipped flow grants those unattended, scoped to environments that actually hold agents.\nSo each collector runs on its own schedule and writes a landing table. The model never calls Purview or Power Automate — it reads Dataverse like any other table.\nLane E — Defender advanced hunting is a GET against one fixed host, so Power BI calls it directly at refresh time. It fails soft: no licence, or no onboarded devices, yields empty tables rather than a broken refresh.\nDrop a lane and every other page still works — you lose only that lane’s pages.\nBoth builds ship the same pages and tables. pbip-cloud\\ refreshes from these lanes live; pbip\\ reads the same shapes from data\\*.csv, including lane E’s Shadow AI signal.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "seed": 285084,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3874973,
      "updated": 1,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lane C — Power BI cannot query the Purview audit API directly: it is POST-only with an Entra audience the Web connector cannot mint.\nLane D — the names live in one Dataverse per environment. Power Query treats 742 endpoints as a dynamic data source and will not refresh them.\nLane D needs a Dataverse application user in every environment first — a second shipped flow grants those unattended, scoped to environments that actually hold agents.\nSo each collector runs on its own schedule and writes a landing table. The model never calls Purview or Power Automate — it reads Dataverse like any other table.\nLane E — Defender advanced hunting is a GET against one fixed host, so Power BI calls it directly at refresh time. It fails soft: no licence, or no onboarded devices, yields empty tables rather than a broken refresh.\nDrop a lane and every other page still works — you lose only that lane’s pages.\nBoth builds ship the same pages and tables. pbip-cloud\\ refreshes from these lanes live; pbip\\ reads the same shapes from data\\*.csv, including lane E’s Shadow AI signal.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false
    },
